## What this notice covers (2026-08-22, revised 2026-08-23 — decisions D-103, D-104)

This file is the **retained upstream notice** for content borrowed from
`babamba2/superclaude-for-sap` (via the frozen `hjaewon/sc4sap-custom`).
It is **not the license of the SAPKIT plugin** — that is the repository root
`LICENSE` (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Hong Jaewon). Nothing above has been altered
and nothing above will be: this section only records what is known about the
subtree it covers.

**It covers the whole `interactive/` subtree.** A 2026-08-22 revision narrowed it
to 36 files; a review found that narrowing counted only one of the two migration
classes, and it was **restored the next day**. A second review found the
replacement count short as well — the ledger's path mapping had never produced a
dozen of the procedure files — so the figures below come from a **reverse scan**
that starts at the files in this tree instead of at the ledger. What is known
today:

| Group | Count | State |
|---|---:|---|
| `server/sap-assets/` | 30 | Upstream, unmodified since import (`copy`). Kept as-is by D-079 ⑥ — these install SAP-side objects that are never renamed or regenerated. **Permanent.** |
| `server/tool-catalog/sc4sap-mcp-tools*.md` · `server/verify-engine.mjs` · `server/bundle-keyring.mjs` | 6 | Upstream (`copy`), still being edited here. Scheduled for replacement. |
| `core/personas/` 25 · `core/procedures/` 16 · adapters 5 · `core/knowledge/` 5 · policies 2 · tools 3 | **56** | Mostly `transform` — **form-converted imports, not rewrites** — plus files the ledger's path mapping never produced. All 56 still share long lines with the upstream original; the personas match on 54–95% of their substantive lines and four procedures on 54–65%. **Not yet accounted for.** |
| Knowledge, industry, country and ABAP-convention content | 170 | Re-authored file by file, each under independent review, finished 2026-08-18. |

The `transform` group is why this notice still covers the whole subtree. Until
each of those files is either re-authored or judged clear, drawing a tighter
boundary would claim authorship the repository cannot support. Progress is
tracked in `docs/reference/copy-baseline.md`; the plan is `docs/BLUEPRINT.md`.
